  "title": "Refusal Behavior in LLMs: Decoding and Exploiting Intermediate Activations",
  "summary": "This paper investigates whether refusal behavior can be predicted from LLM intermediate activations before decoding using linear probes trained on residual stream activations. It reveals that refusal is linearly decodable well before the final layer, suggesting safety-relevant behavior exists in intermediate activations. Mechanistic AutoDAN, a probe-guided variant, enhances attack detection and reduces search time, while demonstrating the utility of probe guidance in AutoDAN-style optimization loops.",
